    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nOccupying a commanding position on Barnhill road this period double-fronted home enjoys an enviable location approximately a short 8 minute walk to the vibrant Town of Dalkey and a short drive to Sandycove and Glasthule villages.\nTraditionally a farmhouse, the property was later extended to the front increasing its original footprint. This spacious residence offers immense potential for a discerning purchaser to complete its transformation into a truly exceptional family home. The property boasts impressive proportions, high ceilings, and glimpses of the sea from the upper floor, laying the foundation for a refined and luxurious living environment.\n\nWhilst the property requires a significant investment to realise its true potential, we believe it will in time be a property of true distinction, elegance and comfort. Set on approximately 0.58 acres, the grounds enjoy exceptional privacy and flexibility, featuring two vehicular entrances, a separate pedestrian gate, a gate lodge and a derelict barn. The extensive outdoor space offers superb potential to develop and upgrade the gate lodge, barn and gardens, (subject to planning permission).\n\nThis highly sought-after address is well served by an array of premier schools including Castlepark, The Harold Boys, Rathdown, Cluny and Loreto Dalkey. The nearby DART provides convenient access to other renowned institutions such as Blackrock College, St. Andrew's College, and St. Michael's.\n\nResidents can also enjoy an abundance of leisure pursuits in the surrounding area, including picturesque coastal and hillside walks, four local sailing clubs, tennis at Sandycove and Glenageary, and golf at Killiney Golf Club.\n\nThis rare offering represents a unique opportunity to craft a dream home in one of Dublin's most desirable coastal enclaves."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Elegant double-fronted residence situated on 0.58-acre site</li><li> Gate Lodge with its own garden</li><li> Prime coastal location close to Dalkey town, Sandycove & Glasthule</li><li>Derelict barn that offers an opportunity for modernisation</li><li> Sea views from upper floors</li><li> Two vehicular entrances and one pedestrian gate</li><li> Within walking distance of Glenageary & Dalkey DART, schools, and recreational</ul>"
      },
